@startuml claim-lifecycle
' How independent findings become one corroborated claim.
' Traced against src/afriend/merge.py (exact_merge) and
' src/afriend/ledger.py.

' Theme: colours sampled from docs/images/brand/afriend-logo-512.png.
' Avenir Next and SF Mono ship with macOS and are absent from the CI runner,
' which only checks that a source renders -- the committed PNG and SVG pair
' is produced by `make diagrams` on a machine that has them.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Avenir Next"
skinparam defaultMonospacedFontName "SF Mono"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #6E8288
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5B7079
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 19
skinparam TitleFontColor #2D424E
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #F8FCFC
skinparam legendBorderColor #A8C3CC
skinparam legendFontSize 12
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F4F1E8
skinparam noteBorderColor #B3AA97
skinparam noteFontColor #4A4436
skinparam noteFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #7E99A3
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF3F4
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #2D424E
skinparam ParticipantFontSize 13
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #7E99A3
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #EAF3F4
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #A8C3CC
skinparam SequenceArrowColor #6E8288

title How corroboration survives deduplication

participant "friend A\nsecurity lens" as A #D9E8D5
participant "friend B\nops lens" as B #D9E8D5
participant "exact_merge" as M
database "claims.jsonl\nappend-only" as L #F6E7C8
participant "report.md" as R

A -> M : claim c-0001\n"the guard is missing"\norigin = [fake/security]
B -> M : claim c-0002\n"The Guard Is  Missing"\norigin = [fake/ops]

note over M
  Dedup key normalizes **only** whitespace
  runs and case, plus a strip on location.
  Nothing else — deliberate under-merge.
end note

M -> M : keys match →\nc-0002 aliases c-0001
M -> M : c-0001.origin grows to\n[fake/security, fake/ops]

M -> L : append claim c-0001
M -> L : append claim c-0002\n<b>(the duplicate too)</b>
M -> L : append alias\ncanonical=c-0001\nduplicate=c-0002

note over L
  The duplicate's own claim record is written,
  not just the alias. Otherwise alias.duplicate
  would dangle and a reader could not rebuild
  corroboration from the ledger alone.
end note

M -> R : one finding, ranked
R -> R : renders\n"corroborated by 2 friends"\nfake/security · fake/ops

note over R #D9E8D5
  Two independent models reaching the same
  conclusion is the strongest signal this
  tool produces — so it is never collapsed
  into a single unattributed claim.
end note

@enduml
